HOW AI ASSISTED OUR PROJECT
Git & GitHub: AI helped us understand commands such as git add, commit, pull, rebase, and push, and helped troubleshoot Git errors when uploading our work.
Web Redesign: AI helped convert the original Python functions into a Flask web application and connect Register Patient, Appointment, Billing and Triage.
Input Validation: AI helped improve rules such as the P000 Patient ID format, age limit, department selection and appointment-date validation.
Docker: AI helped explain Dockerfiles, images, containers, isolated environments and how the CareBridge application can be packaged and run consistently.
ngrok: If your team used AI for this part, add: “AI helped us understand how ngrok exposes a locally running website through a temporary public URL.”

CHALLENGES & HOW AI HELPED
GitHub push and repository errors → AI guided us through the correct Git commands.
Flask/package errors → AI helped identify missing packages and incorrect folder paths.
Separate Python functions → AI helped integrate them into one connected system.
Changing project requirements → AI helped update the pseudocode, Python code and web validation.
Docker concepts were unfamiliar → AI helped explain the process in simpler terms.
Deployment/testing issues → AI helped us understand what to check and how the tools connect.

KEY TAKEAWAYS
Learned how Git and GitHub support team collaboration.
Learned how HTML, CSS, Flask and Python work together in a web application.
Learned the purpose of Docker images and containers.
Learned how local applications can be shared using tools such as ngrok.
Improved our ability to troubleshoot technical problems.
Learned that AI can speed up development, but the output still needs to be tested and checked against the project requirements.
